VALUES
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 1, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Let $\alpha, \alpha+2$, $\alpha \in \mathbb{Z}$, be the roots of the quadratic equation $x(x+2)+(x+1)(x+3)+(x+2)(x+4)+\dots+(x+n-1)(x+n+1)=40n$ for some $n \in \mathbb{N}$. Then $n+\alpha$ is equal to:', '[{"key":"A","text":"0"},{"key":"B","text":"1"},{"key":"C","text":"2"},{"key":"D","text":"3"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'EASY', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002', 2, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Let $x$ and $y$ be real numbers such that $50\left(\frac{2x}{1+3i}-\frac{y}{1-2i}\right)=31+17i$, $i=\sqrt{-1}$. Then the value of $10(x-3y)$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"20"},{"key":"B","text":"31"},{"key":"C","text":"35"},{"key":"D","text":"75"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'MEDIUM', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003', 3, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Let $\alpha,\beta \in \mathbb{R}$ be such that the system of linear equations:
$x+2y+z=5$
$2x+y+\alpha z=5$
$8x+4y+\beta z=18$
has no solution. Then $\frac{\beta}{\alpha}$ is equal to:', '[{"key":"A","text":"-4"},{"key":"B","text":"4"},{"key":"C","text":"8"},{"key":"D","text":"-8"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'HARD', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004', 4, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Let $A=\begin{bmatrix}1&2\\ 1&\alpha\end{bmatrix}$ and $B=\begin{bmatrix}3&3\\ \beta&2\end{bmatrix}$. If $A^2-4A+I=O$ and $B^2-5B-6I=O$, then among the two statements:
(S1): $[(B-A)(B+A)]^T=\begin{bmatrix}13&15\\ 7&10\end{bmatrix}$
(S2): $\det(\text{adj}(A+B))=-5$:', '[{"key":"A","text":"only (S1) is correct"},{"key":"B","text":"only (S2) is correct"},{"key":"C","text":"both (S1) and (S2) are correct"},{"key":"D","text":"both (S1) and (S2) are wrong"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'EASY', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005', 5, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Let A be the set of first 101 terms of an A.P., whose first term is 1 and the common difference is 5 and let B be the set of first 71 terms of an A.P., whose first term is 9 and the common difference is 7. Then the number of elements in $A \cap B$, which are divisible by 3, is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"4"},{"key":"B","text":"5"},{"key":"C","text":"6"},{"key":"D","text":"7"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'MEDIUM', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006', 6, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'The number of seven-digit numbers, that can be formed by using the digits 1, 2, 3, 5 and 7 such that each digit is used at least once, is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"15400"},{"key":"B","text":"17800"},{"key":"C","text":"16800"},{"key":"D","text":"29400"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'HARD', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007', 7, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'The number of elements in the set $S=\left\{(r,k): k \in \mathbb{Z} \text{ and } {}^{36}C_{r+1} = \frac{6({}^{35}C_r)}{k^2-3}\right\}$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"2"},{"key":"B","text":"4"},{"key":"C","text":"8"},{"key":"D","text":"16"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'EASY', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000008', 8, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'If the mean of the data:
Class: 5-10 | 10-15 | 15-20 | 20-25 | 25-30 | 30-35
Frequency: 2 | k | 28 | 54 | k+1 | 5
is 21, then k is one of the roots of the equation:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$2x^2-23x-10=0$"},{"key":"B","text":"$4x^2-35x+24=0$"},{"key":"C","text":"$2x^2-19x-10=0$"},{"key":"D","text":"$2x^2-35x+98=0$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'MEDIUM', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009', 9, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Let the mid points of the sides of a triangle ABC be $(\frac{5}{2},7)$, $(\frac{5}{2},3)$ and $(4,5)$. If its incentre is $(h, k)$, then $3h+k$ is equal to:', '[{"key":"A","text":"11"},{"key":"B","text":"12"},{"key":"C","text":"13"},{"key":"D","text":"14"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'HARD', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000010', 10, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Let an ellipse $\frac{x^2}{a^2}+\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1$, $a<b$, pass through the point $(4,3)$ and have eccentricity $\frac{\sqrt{5}}{3}$. Then the length of its latus rectum is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{3}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$2\\sqrt{5}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{7\\sqrt{5}}{3}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{8\\sqrt{5}}{3}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'EASY', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011', 11, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'If $\sin\left(\frac{\pi}{18}\right)\sin\left(\frac{5\pi}{18}\right)\sin\left(\frac{7\pi}{18}\right)=K$, then the value of $\sin\left(\frac{10K\pi}{3}\right)$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+1}{2\\sqrt{2}}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{\\sqrt{2}}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{1}{2}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'MEDIUM', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012', 12, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Let $S=\{x \in [-\pi,\pi]: \sin x(\sin x+\cos x)=a, a \in \mathbb{Z}\}$. Then $n(S)$ is equal to:', '[{"key":"A","text":"3"},{"key":"B","text":"6"},{"key":"C","text":"7"},{"key":"D","text":"9"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'HARD', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000013', 13, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'If the point of intersection of the lines $\frac{x+1}{3}=\frac{y+a}{5}=\frac{z+b+1}{7}$ and $\frac{x-2}{1}=\frac{y-b}{4}=\frac{z-2a}{7}$ lies on xy-plane, then the value of $a+b$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"2"},{"key":"B","text":"5"},{"key":"C","text":"7"},{"key":"D","text":"9"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'EASY', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014', 14, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'If $\vec{a}$ and $\vec{b}$ are two vectors such that $|\vec{a}|=2$ and $|\vec{b}|=3$, then the maximum value of $3|(3\vec{a}+2\vec{b})|+4|(3\vec{a}-2\vec{b})|$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"30"},{"key":"B","text":"36"},{"key":"C","text":"60"},{"key":"D","text":"72"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'MEDIUM', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015', 15, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Let a line L passing through the point $(1, 1, 1)$ be perpendicular to both the vectors $2\hat{i}+2\hat{j}+\hat{k}$ and $\hat{i}+2\hat{j}+2\hat{k}$. If $P(a,b,c)$ is the foot of perpendicular from the origin on the line L, then the value of $34(a+b+c)$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"50"},{"key":"B","text":"80"},{"key":"C","text":"100"},{"key":"D","text":"120"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'HARD', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000016', 16, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'If $\lim_{x\rightarrow 2}\frac{\sin(x^3-5x^2+ax+b)}{(\sqrt{x-1}-1)\log_e(x-1)}=m$, then $a+b+m$ is equal to:', '[{"key":"A","text":"5"},{"key":"B","text":"6"},{"key":"C","text":"8"},{"key":"D","text":"10"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'EASY', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000017', 17, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'If the curve $y=f(x)$ passes through the point $(1, e)$ and satisfies the differential equation $dy=y(2+\log_e x)dx$, $x>0$, then $f(e)$ is equal to:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$e$"},{"key":"B","text":"$e^{e^2}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$e^{2e}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$e^{3e}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'MEDIUM', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000018', 18, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'The number of critical points of the function $f(x)=\begin{cases}|\frac{\sin x}{x}|, & x \ne 0 \\ 1, & x=0\end{cases}$ in the interval $(-2\pi,2\pi)$ is equal to:', '[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"3"},{"key":"C","text":"5"},{"key":"D","text":"7"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'HARD', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000019', 19, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Let $[\cdot]$ denote the greatest integer function. Then the value of $\int_{0}^{3}\left(\frac{e^x+e^{-x}}{[x]!}\right)dx$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$e^2+e^3-\\frac{1}{e^2}-\\frac{1}{e^3}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{1}{2}\\left(e^2+e^3-\\frac{1}{e^2}-\\frac{1}{e^3}\\right)$"},{"key":"C","text":"$e^2+e^3-\\frac{1}{2e^2}-\\frac{1}{2e^3}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{1}{2}(e^2+e^3)-\\frac{1}{e^2}-\\frac{1}{e^3}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'EASY', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000020', 20, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Let $y=y(x)$ be the solution curve of the differential equation $(1+\sin x)\frac{dy}{dx}+(y+1)\cos x=0; y(0)=0$. If the curve $y=y(x)$ passes through the point $(\alpha,-\frac{1}{2})$, then a value of $\alpha$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{\\pi}{6}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{\\pi}{3}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'MEDIUM', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000021', 21, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'If the domain of the function $f(x)=\sqrt{\log_{(0.6)}\left(|\frac{2x-5}{x^2-4}|\right)}$ is $(-\infty,a]\cup\{b\}\cup[c,d)\cup(e,\infty)$, then the value of $a+b+c+d+e$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"Option A"},{"key":"B","text":"Option B"},{"key":"C","text":"Option C"},{"key":"D","text":"Option D"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'HARD', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000022', 22, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'If $\sum_{k=1}^{n}a_k=6n^3$, then $\sum_{k=1}^{6}\left(\frac{a_{k+1}-a_k}{36}\right)^2$ is equal to:', '[{"key":"A","text":"Option A"},{"key":"B","text":"Option B"},{"key":"C","text":"Option C"},{"key":"D","text":"Option D"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"91","key":"91"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'EASY', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000023', 23, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Let $a, b, c \in \{1,2,3,4\}$. If the probability that $ax^2+2\sqrt{2}bx+c>0$ for all $x \in \mathbb{R}$ is $\frac{m}{n}$, where $\gcd(m,n)=1$, then $m+n$ is equal to:', '[{"key":"A","text":"Option A"},{"key":"B","text":"Option B"},{"key":"C","text":"Option C"},{"key":"D","text":"Option D"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"81","key":"81"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'MEDIUM', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000024', 24, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Let a circle C have its centre in the first quadrant, intersect the coordinate axes at exactly three points and cut off equal intercepts from the coordinate axes. If the length of the chord of C on the line $x+y=1$ is $\sqrt{14}$, then the square of the radius of C is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"Option A"},{"key":"B","text":"Option B"},{"key":"C","text":"Option C"},{"key":"D","text":"Option D"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"8","key":"8"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'HARD', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000025', 25, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'If $\alpha=\int_{0}^{2\sqrt{3}}\log_2(x^2+4)dx+\int_{2}^{4}\sqrt{2^x-4}dx$, then $\alpha^2$ is equal to:', '[{"key":"A","text":"Option A"},{"key":"B","text":"Option B"},{"key":"C","text":"Option C"},{"key":"D","text":"Option D"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"192","key":"192"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Mathematics.', 'EASY', 'Mathematics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000026', 26, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'The dimensional formula of $\frac{1}{2}\epsilon_0 E^2$ ($\epsilon_0=$ permittivity of vacuum and $E=$ electric field) is $M^a L^b T^c$. The value of $2a-b+c$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"0"},{"key":"B","text":"1"},{"key":"C","text":"-1"},{"key":"D","text":"2"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'MEDIUM', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000027', 27, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'The diameter of a wire measured by a screw gauge of least count 0.001 cm is 0.08 cm. The length measured by a scale of least count 0.1 cm is 150 cm. When a weight of 100 N is applied to the wire, the extension in length is 0.5 cm, measured by a micrometer of least count 0.001 cm. The error in the measured Young''s modulus is $\alpha\times10^{9}\text{ N/m}^2$. The value of $\alpha$ is (Ignore the contribution of the load to Young''s modulus error calculation):', '[{"key":"A","text":"1.3"},{"key":"B","text":"1.65"},{"key":"C","text":"0.13"},{"key":"D","text":"0.25"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'HARD', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000028', 28, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'The velocity of a particle is given as $\vec{v}=-x\hat{i}+2y\hat{j}-z\hat{k}\text{ m/s}$. The magnitude of acceleration at point $(1, 2, 4)$ is ___ $\text{m/s}^2$.', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\sqrt{6}$"},{"key":"B","text":"9"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\sqrt{33}$"},{"key":"D","text":"0"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'EASY', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000029', 29, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'The position of an object having mass 0.1 kg as a function of time t is given as $\vec{r}=(10t^2\hat{i}+5t^3\hat{j})\text{ m}$. At $t=1\text{ s}$, which of the following statements are correct?
A. The linear momentum $\vec{p}=(2\hat{i}+1.5\hat{j})\text{ kg}\cdot\text{m/s}$.
B. The force acting on the object $\vec{F}=(2\hat{i}+3\hat{j})\text{ N}$.
C. The angular momentum of the object about its origin $\vec{L}=15\hat{k}\text{ J}\cdot\text{s}$.
D. The torque acting on the object about its origin $\vec{\tau}=20\hat{k}\text{ N}\cdot\text{m}$.
Choose the correct answer from the options given below:', '[{"key":"A","text":"A, B and C only"},{"key":"B","text":"B, C and D only"},{"key":"C","text":"A, C and D only"},{"key":"D","text":"A, B and D only"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'MEDIUM', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000030', 30, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'A planet ($P_1$) is moving around the star of mass $2M$ in the orbit of radius $R$. Another planet ($P_2$) is moving around another star of mass $4M$ in an orbit of radius $2R$. Ratio of time periods of revolution of $P_2$ and $P_1$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{1}{2}$"},{"key":"B","text":"2"},{"key":"C","text":"4"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{1}{4}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'HARD', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000031', 31, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'A particle is rotating in a circular path and at any instant its motion can be described as $\theta=\frac{5t^4}{40}-\frac{t^3}{3}$. The angular acceleration of the particle after 10 seconds is ___ $\text{rad/s}^2$:', '[{"key":"A","text":"150"},{"key":"B","text":"120"},{"key":"C","text":"130"},{"key":"D","text":"170"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'EASY', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000032', 32, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'A parallel plate air capacitor has a capacitance C. When it is half filled as shown in figure with a dielectric constant $K=5$, the percentage increase in the capacitance is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"33.34"},{"key":"B","text":"66.67"},{"key":"C","text":"200"},{"key":"D","text":"400"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'MEDIUM', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', '/diagrams/q32_capacitor_dielectric.png'),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000033', 33, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Heat is supplied to a diatomic gas at constant pressure. Then the ratio of $\Delta Q:\Delta U:\Delta W$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"2:3:5"},{"key":"B","text":"5:3:2"},{"key":"C","text":"2:5:7"},{"key":"D","text":"7:5:2"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'HARD', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000034', 34, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Two charged conducting spheres $S_1$ and $S_2$ of radii 8 cm and 18 cm are connected to each other by a wire. After equilibrium is established, the ratio of electric fields on $S_1$ and $S_2$ spheres are $E_{S_1}$ and $E_{S_2}$ respectively. The value of $\frac{E_{S_1}}{E_{S_2}}$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{3}{2}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{2}{3}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{4}{9}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{9}{4}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'EASY', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000035', 35, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'The equation of a plane progressive wave is given by $y=5\cos\pi\left(200t-\frac{x}{150}\right)$, where $x$ and $y$ are in cm and $t$ is in second. The velocity of the wave is ___ $\text{m/s}$:', '[{"key":"A","text":"120"},{"key":"B","text":"150"},{"key":"C","text":"200"},{"key":"D","text":"300"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'MEDIUM', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000036', 36, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Two short electric dipoles A and B having dipole moment $p_1$ and $p_2$ respectively are placed with their axis mutually perpendicular as shown in the figure. The resultant electric field at a point z is making an angle of $60^{\circ}$ with the line joining points O and z. The ratio of the dipole moments $p_2/p_1$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$2\\sqrt{3}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\sqrt{3}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'HARD', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', '/diagrams/q36_dipoles.png'),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000037', 37, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'For the given circuit (shown in part (A)) the time dependent input voltage $v_{in}(t)$ and corresponding output $v_o(t)$ are shown in part (B) and part (C), respectively. Identify the components that are used in the circuit between points X and Y.', '[{"key":"A","text":"Series Resistor connected to terminal Y"},{"key":"B","text":"Parallel Diode and Inductor"},{"key":"C","text":"Single Zener Diode with opposite polarity"},{"key":"D","text":"Series Resistor and opposite back-to-back Zener network"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'EASY', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', '/diagrams/q37_zener_circuit.png'),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000038', 38, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'When a coil is placed in a time dependent magnetic field the power dissipated in it is P. The number of turns, area of the coil and radius of the coil wire are N, A and r respectively. For a second coil, number of turns, area of the coil and radius of the coil wire are 2N, 2A and 3r respectively. When the first coil is replaced with second coil the power dissipated in it is $\sqrt{2}\alpha P$. The value of $\alpha$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"36"},{"key":"B","text":"$128\\sqrt{2}$"},{"key":"C","text":"16"},{"key":"D","text":"64"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'MEDIUM', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000039', 39, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Two identical long current carrying wires are bent into the shapes shown in the following figures. If the magnitude of magnetic fields at the centres P and Q of a semicircular arc are $B_1$ and $B_2$ respectively, then the ratio $\frac{B_1}{B_2}$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{2+\\pi}{1+\\pi}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{1+\\pi}{1-\\pi}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{2+\\pi}{1-\\pi}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{1+\\pi}{2-\\pi}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'HARD', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', '/diagrams/q39_wire_loops.png'),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000040', 40, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'For a thin symmetric prism made of glass (refractive index 1.5), the ratio of incident angle and minimum deviation will be:', '[{"key":"A","text":"3:4"},{"key":"B","text":"3:2"},{"key":"C","text":"2:1"},{"key":"D","text":"1:2"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'EASY', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000041', 41, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Refer the figure given below. $\mu_1$ and $\mu_2$ are refractive indices of air and lens material. The height of image will be ___ cm.', '[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"0.5"},{"key":"C","text":"1.2"},{"key":"D","text":"0.25"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'MEDIUM', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', '/diagrams/q41_refraction_curved_surface.png'),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000042', 42, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'For a certain metal, when monochromatic light of wavelength $\lambda$ is incident, the stopping potential for photoelectrons is $3V_0$. When the same metal is illuminated by light of wavelength $2\lambda$, then the stopping potential becomes $V_0$. The threshold wavelength for photoelectric emission for the given metal is $\alpha\lambda$. The value of $\alpha$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"4"},{"key":"C","text":"2"},{"key":"D","text":"3"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'HARD', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000043', 43, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'An electromagnetic wave travelling in x-direction is described by field equation $E_y=300\sin\omega\left(t-\frac{x}{c}\right)$. If the electron is restricted to move in y-direction only with speed of $1.5\times10^{6}\text{ m/s}$, then ratio of maximum electric and magnetic forces acting on the electron is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"200"},{"key":"B","text":"150"},{"key":"C","text":"400"},{"key":"D","text":"300"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'EASY', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000044', 44, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Angular momentum of an electron in a hydrogen atom is $\frac{3h}{\pi}$, then the energy of the electron is ___ eV.', '[{"key":"A","text":"-1.51"},{"key":"B","text":"-0.85"},{"key":"C","text":"-0.38"},{"key":"D","text":"-0.28"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'MEDIUM', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000045', 45, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'A liquid drop of diameter 2 mm breaks into 512 droplets. The change in surface energy is $\alpha\times10^{-6}\text{ J}$. The value of $\alpha$ is (Take surface tension of liquid $=0.08\text{ N/m}$):', '[{"key":"A","text":"10"},{"key":"B","text":"7"},{"key":"C","text":"8"},{"key":"D","text":"11"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'HARD', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000046', 46, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'In single slit diffraction pattern, the wavelength of light used is 628 nm and slit width is 0.2 mm, the angular width of central maximum is $\alpha\times10^{-2}$ degrees. The value of $\alpha$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"Option A"},{"key":"B","text":"Option B"},{"key":"C","text":"Option C"},{"key":"D","text":"Option D"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"36","key":"36"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'EASY', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000047', 47, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'A vessel contains $0.15\text{ m}^3$ of a gas at pressure 8 bar and temperature $140^{\circ}\text{C}$ with $c_p=3R$ and $c_v=2R$. It is expanded adiabatically till pressure falls to 1 bar. The work done during this process is ___ kJ. (R is gas constant)', '[{"key":"A","text":"Option A"},{"key":"B","text":"Option B"},{"key":"C","text":"Option C"},{"key":"D","text":"Option D"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"120","key":"120"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'MEDIUM', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000048', 48, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'A $1\ \mu\text{C}$ charge is moving with velocity $\vec{v}=(\hat{i}-2\hat{j}+3\hat{k})\text{ m/s}$ in the region of magnetic field $\vec{B}=(2\hat{i}+3\hat{j}-5\hat{k})\text{ T}$. The magnitude of force acting on it is $\sqrt{\alpha}\times10^{-6}\text{ N}$. The value of $\alpha$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"Option A"},{"key":"B","text":"Option B"},{"key":"C","text":"Option C"},{"key":"D","text":"Option D"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"171","key":"171"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'HARD', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000049', 49, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'A uniform wire of length $l$ of weight $w$ is suspended from the roof with a weight of $W$ at the other end. The stress in the wire at $\frac{l}{3}$ distance from the top is $\left(\frac{W}{A}+\frac{2}{\gamma}\frac{w}{A}\right)$, where A is the cross sectional area of the wire. The value of $\gamma$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"Option A"},{"key":"B","text":"Option B"},{"key":"C","text":"Option C"},{"key":"D","text":"Option D"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'EASY', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000050', 50, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'A tub is filled with water and a wooden cube $10\text{ cm}\times10\text{ cm}\times10\text{ cm}$ is placed in the water. The wooden cube is found to float on the water with a part of it submerged in water. When a metal coin is placed on the wooden cube, the submerged part is increased by 3.87 cm. The mass of the metal coin is ___ gram. (Take water density as $1\text{ g/cm}^3$ and density of wood as $0.4\text{ g/cm}^3$)', '[{"key":"A","text":"Option A"},{"key":"B","text":"Option B"},{"key":"C","text":"Option C"},{"key":"D","text":"Option D"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"387","key":"387"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Physics.', 'MEDIUM', 'Physics Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000051', 51, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'The mass of iron converted into $\text{Fe}_3\text{O}_4$ by the action of 18 g of steam is :
