  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000058', 58, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '$t_{100\%}$ is the time required for the 100% completion of the reaction while $t_{1/2}$ is the time required for 50% of the reaction to be completed. Which of the following options correctly represents the relation between $t_{100\%}$ and $t_{1/2}$ for zero and first order reactions respectively?', '[{"key":"A","text":"$t_{100\\%}=(t_{1/2})^2$ and $t_{100\\%}=(t_{1/2})^{-\\infty}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$t_{100\\%}=2t_{1/2}$ and $t_{100\\%}=(t_{1/2})^{\\infty}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$t_{100\\%}=2t_{1/2}$ and $t_{100\\%}=(2t_{1/2})^2$"},{"key":"D","text":"$t_{100\\%}=(t_{1/2})^{\\infty}$ and $t_{100\\%}=2t_{1/2}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Chemistry.', 'EASY', 'Chemistry Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000059', 59, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Given below are two statements:
