Choose the correct answer from the options given below:', '[{"key":"A","text":"A-IV, B-II, C-I, D-III"},{"key":"B","text":"A-IV, B-II, C-III, D-I"},{"key":"C","text":"A-II, B-IV, C-I, D-III"},{"key":"D","text":"A-II, B-IV, C-III, D-I"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Chemistry.', 'EASY', 'Chemistry Comprehensive Core', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000068', 68, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Consider the three aromatic molecules (P: N,N-dimethylaniline; Q: N,N,2-trimethylaniline; R: N,N,2,6-tetramethylaniline). The correct order regarding the reactivity of these compounds with $\text{Ph}-\text{N}\equiv\text{N}^+\text{Cl}^-$ under optimum but slightly acidic medium is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$P > Q > R$"},{"key":"B","text":"$R > P > Q$"},{"key":"C","text":"$R > Q > P$"},{"key":"D","text":"$P > R > Q$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, 'Standard solution by method of deduction for Chemistry.', 'MEDIUM', 'Chemistry Comprehensive Core', '/diagrams/q68_amines_coupling.png'),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000069', 69, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, 'Match List - I with List - II.

