  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000157', 157, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q157] Evaluate: $\lim_{x \to 0} \frac{e^{\sin x} - 1 - \sin x}{x^2}$.', '[{"key":"A","text":"$1$"},{"key":"B","text":"$0$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{1}{4}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{1}{2}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, 'Using series expansion $e^t = 1 + t + \frac{t^2}{2!} + \dots$, $\frac{t^2/2}{x^2} \to 1/2$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Limits & Continuity', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000158', 158, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q158] The de Broglie wavelength of an electron accelerated through a potential difference of $100$ V is approximately:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$1.23$ nm"},{"key":"B","text":"$0.012$ nm"},{"key":"C","text":"$0.123$ nm"},{"key":"D","text":"$12.3$ nm"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, '$\lambda = \frac{1.227}{\sqrt{V}}$ nm $= \frac{1.227}{10} = 0.123$ nm.', 'HARD', 'Modern Physics', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000159', 159, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q159] Which of the following nitrogenous bases is found in RNA but not in DNA?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Thymine"},{"key":"B","text":"Uracil"},{"key":"C","text":"Guanine"},{"key":"D","text":"Cytosine"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'RNA contains Uracil instead of Thymine.', 'EASY', 'Biomolecules', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000160', 160, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q160] Evaluate the definite integral: $I = \int_{0}^{\pi/2} \frac{\sin^3 x}{\sin^3 x + \cos^3 x} dx$', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\pi$"},{"key":"D","text":"$0$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, 'By applying property $\int_a^b f(x)dx = \int_a^b f(a+b-x)dx$, $2I = \int_0^{\pi/2} 1 dx = \frac{\pi}{2} \implies I = \frac{\pi}{4}$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Definite Integrals', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000161', 161, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q161] The electric potential at a distance $r$ from an electric dipole on its axial line varies as:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{1}{r}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{1}{r^3}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$r^2$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{1}{r^2}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, '$V_{\text{axial}} = \frac{1}{4\pi \epsilon_0} \frac{p}{r^2}$.', 'HARD', 'Electrostatics', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000162', 162, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q162] The hybridization and magnetic character of $[\text{Ni}(\text{CN})_4]^{2-}$ complex ion are:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$sp^3$, Paramagnetic"},{"key":"B","text":"$dsp^2$, Paramagnetic"},{"key":"C","text":"$dsp^2$, Diamagnetic"},{"key":"D","text":"$sp^3$, Diamagnetic"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, '$\text{CN}^-$ is a strong field ligand causing pairing of $3d^8$ electrons into square planar $dsp^2$, leaving no unpaired electrons.', 'EASY', 'Coordination Compounds', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000163', 163, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q163] The general solution of the differential equation $\frac{dy}{dx} + y \tan x = \sec x$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$y \\cos x = \\sin x + C$"},{"key":"B","text":"$y \\sec x = \\tan x + C$"},{"key":"C","text":"$y = \\sin x + C \\cos x$"},{"key":"D","text":"$y = \\tan x + C \\sec x$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, '$\text{I.F.} = e^{\int \tan x dx} = \sec x$. Solution is $y \cdot \sec x = \int \sec^2 x dx + C = \tan x + C$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Differential Equations', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000164', 164, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q164] An ideal Carnot heat engine operates between temperatures $500$ K and $300$ K. Its thermal efficiency is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$40\\%$"},{"key":"B","text":"$60\\%$"},{"key":"C","text":"$50\\%$"},{"key":"D","text":"$30\\%$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, '$\eta = 1 - \frac{T_C}{T_H} = 1 - \frac{300}{500} = 0.4 = 40\%$.', 'HARD', 'Thermodynamics', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000165', 165, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q165] For an endothermic reaction to be spontaneous at all temperatures, the change in entropy $\Delta S$ must be:', '[{"key":"A","text":"Negative"},{"key":"B","text":"Zero"},{"key":"C","text":"Always non-spontaneous"},{"key":"D","text":"Positive and $T\\Delta S > \\Delta H$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, '$\Delta G = \Delta H - T\Delta S$. For spontaneity $\Delta G < 0$, requiring $\Delta S > 0$ and $T\Delta S > \Delta H$.', 'EASY', 'Thermodynamics', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000166', 166, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q166] The distance of the point $(1, 2, 3)$ from the plane $2x + y - 2z + 9 = 0$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$2$"},{"key":"B","text":"$7$"},{"key":"C","text":"$3$"},{"key":"D","text":"$1$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, '$d = \frac{|2(1) + 1(2) - 2(3) + 9|}{\sqrt{4+1+4}} = \frac{|2+2-6+9|}{3} = \frac{7}{3}$.', 'MEDIUM', '3D Geometry', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000167', 167, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q167] The escape velocity from the surface of Earth is $11.2$ km/s. If a planet has twice the mass and twice the radius of Earth, its escape velocity is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$22.4$ km/s"},{"key":"B","text":"$11.2$ km/s"},{"key":"C","text":"$5.6$ km/s"},{"key":"D","text":"$15.8$ km/s"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, '$v_e = \sqrt{\frac{2GM}{R}}$. If $M$ and $R$ both double, $M/R$ remains constant, so $v_e$ is unchanged.', 'HARD', 'Gravitation', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000168', 168, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q168] For a first-order reaction $A \to \text{Products}$, the half-life period is $69.3$ minutes. The rate constant $k$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$0.01 \\; \\text{min}^{-1}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$0.1 \\; \\text{min}^{-1}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$0.001 \\; \\text{min}^{-1}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$1.0 \\; \\text{min}^{-1}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, '$k = \frac{0.693}{t_{1/2}} = \frac{0.693}{69.3} = 0.01 \; \text{min}^{-1}$.', 'EASY', 'Chemical Kinetics', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000169', 169, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q169] If $A$ is a $3 \times 3$ non-singular matrix such that $|A| = 4$, then find the value of $|\text{adj}(2A)|$.', '[{"key":"A","text":"1024"},{"key":"B","text":"2048"},{"key":"C","text":"512"},{"key":"D","text":"4096"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, '$|\text{adj}(2A)| = |2A|^{n-1} = (2^3 |A|)^2 = (8 \times 4)^2 = 32^2 = 1024$... check order $n=3$, $(2^3 \cdot 4)^2 = 32^2 = 1024$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Matrices & Determinants', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000170', 170, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q170] A wire of resistance $16 \; \Omega$ is stretched uniformly to twice its original length. The new resistance of the wire will be:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$32 \\; \\Omega$"},{"key":"B","text":"$16 \\; \\Omega$"},{"key":"C","text":"$64 \\; \\Omega$"},{"key":"D","text":"$8 \\; \\Omega$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, '$R \propto l^2$ when volume is conserved. Since length doubles, $R'' = 4 R = 64 \; \Omega$.', 'HARD', 'Current Electricity', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000171', 171, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q171] Which of the following compounds gives a positive Iodoform test upon reaction with $\text{I}_2 / \text{NaOH}$?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Methanol ($\\text{CH}_3\\text{OH}$)"},{"key":"B","text":"Ethanol ($\\text{CH}_3\\text{CH}_2\\text{OH}$)"},{"key":"C","text":"Benzaldehyde"},{"key":"D","text":"Diethyl ether"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'Ethanol has the $\text{CH}_3\text{CH(OH)}-$ unit which oxidizes to acetaldehyde containing $\text{CH}_3\text{C=O}$, giving yellow $\text{CHI}_3$ precipitate.', 'EASY', 'Organic Chemistry (Aldehydes)', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000172', 172, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q172] Two dice are thrown simultaneously. The probability that the sum of the numbers appearing on the dice is a prime number is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{5}{12}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{7}{18}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{1}{3}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{1}{2}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, 'Prime sums: 2 (1), 3 (2), 5 (4), 7 (6), 11 (2) = total 15 outcomes. $P = 15/36 = 5/12$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Probability', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000173', 173, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q173] In Young’s double-slit experiment, if the distance between the slits is halved and the screen distance is doubled, the fringe width becomes:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$2$ times"},{"key":"B","text":"Halved"},{"key":"C","text":"Unchanged"},{"key":"D","text":"$4$ times"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, '$\beta = \frac{\lambda D}{d}$. If $D'' = 2D$ and $d'' = d/2$, $\beta'' = 4 \beta$.', 'HARD', 'Wave Optics', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000174', 174, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q174] The basicity of orthophosphoric acid ($\text{H}_3\text{PO}_4$) is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$2$"},{"key":"B","text":"$1$"},{"key":"C","text":"$3$"},{"key":"D","text":"$4$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, '$\text{H}_3\text{PO}_4$ has three $\text{P-OH}$ ionizable protons, hence basicity is 3.', 'EASY', 'p-Block Elements', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000175', 175, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q175] If $|z - 4/z| = 2$, then the maximum value of $|z|$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\sqrt{5} - 1$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\sqrt{5} + 1$"},{"key":"C","text":"$2\\sqrt{5}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\sqrt{3} + 1$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'By triangle inequality, $|z| - 4/|z| \le |z - 4/z| = 2 \implies |z|^2 - 2|z| - 4 \le 0 \implies |z| \le \sqrt{5}+1$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Complex Numbers', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000176', 176, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q176] A solid sphere and a hollow sphere of equal mass and radius roll down an inclined plane without slipping. The ratio of their accelerations is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{25}{21}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{21}{25}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{15}{14}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{14}{15}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, '$a = \frac{g \sin \theta}{1 + I/(mR^2)}$. For solid: $a_1 = \frac{5}{7}g \sin \theta$. For hollow: $a_2 = \frac{3}{5}g \sin \theta$. Ratio $= \frac{25}{21}$.', 'HARD', 'Rotational Motion', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000177', 177, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q177] Standard electrode potential $E^\circ$ for $\text{Zn}^{2+}/\text{Zn}$ is $-0.76$ V and for $\text{Cu}^{2+}/\text{Cu}$ is $+0.34$ V. The cell EMF $E^\circ_{\text{cell}}$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$-1.10$ V"},{"key":"B","text":"$+0.42$ V"},{"key":"C","text":"$-0.42$ V"},{"key":"D","text":"$+1.10$ V"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, '$E^\circ_{\text{cell}} = E^\circ_{\text{cathode}} - E^\circ_{\text{anode}} = 0.34 - (-0.76) = 1.10$ V.', 'EASY', 'Electrochemistry', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000178', 178, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q178] Let $\vec{a} = 2\hat{i} + \hat{j} - 2\hat{k}$ and $\vec{b} = \hat{i} + \hat{j}$. The projection of $\vec{a}$ along $\vec{b}$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{3}{2}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\sqrt{2}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$3\\sqrt{2}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, '$\text{proj}_{\vec{b}} \vec{a} = \frac{\vec{a} \cdot \vec{b}}{|\vec{b}|} = \frac{2(1) + 1(1) + 0}{\sqrt{1^2+1^2}} = \frac{3}{\sqrt{2}}$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Vector Algebra', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000179', 179, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q179] The magnetic flux linked with a coil varies with time as $\Phi = 4t^3 - 2t + 5$ Wb. The magnitude of induced EMF at $t = 2$ s is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$48$ V"},{"key":"B","text":"$46$ V"},{"key":"C","text":"$50$ V"},{"key":"D","text":"$44$ V"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, '$e = |-\frac{d\Phi}{dt}| = |12t^2 - 2|$. At $t=2$, $e = 12(4) - 2 = 46$ V.', 'HARD', 'Electromagnetic Induction', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000180', 180, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q180] The van ''t Hoff factor $i$ for a dilute aqueous solution of barium chloride $\text{BaCl}_2$ assuming complete dissociation is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$3$"},{"key":"B","text":"$2$"},{"key":"C","text":"$1$"},{"key":"D","text":"$4$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, '$\text{BaCl}_2 \to \text{Ba}^{2+} + 2\text{Cl}^-$, producing 3 ions per formula unit.', 'EASY', 'Solutions', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000181', 181, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q181] Evaluate: $\lim_{x \to 0} \frac{e^{\sin x} - 1 - \sin x}{x^2}$.', '[{"key":"A","text":"$1$"},{"key":"B","text":"$0$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{1}{4}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{1}{2}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, 'Using series expansion $e^t = 1 + t + \frac{t^2}{2!} + \dots$, $\frac{t^2/2}{x^2} \to 1/2$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Limits & Continuity', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000182', 182, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q182] The de Broglie wavelength of an electron accelerated through a potential difference of $100$ V is approximately:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$1.23$ nm"},{"key":"B","text":"$0.012$ nm"},{"key":"C","text":"$0.123$ nm"},{"key":"D","text":"$12.3$ nm"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, '$\lambda = \frac{1.227}{\sqrt{V}}$ nm $= \frac{1.227}{10} = 0.123$ nm.', 'HARD', 'Modern Physics', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000183', 183, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q183] Which of the following nitrogenous bases is found in RNA but not in DNA?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Thymine"},{"key":"B","text":"Uracil"},{"key":"C","text":"Guanine"},{"key":"D","text":"Cytosine"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'RNA contains Uracil instead of Thymine.', 'EASY', 'Biomolecules', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000184', 184, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q184] Evaluate the definite integral: $I = \int_{0}^{\pi/2} \frac{\sin^3 x}{\sin^3 x + \cos^3 x} dx$', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\pi$"},{"key":"D","text":"$0$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, 'By applying property $\int_a^b f(x)dx = \int_a^b f(a+b-x)dx$, $2I = \int_0^{\pi/2} 1 dx = \frac{\pi}{2} \implies I = \frac{\pi}{4}$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Definite Integrals', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000185', 185, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q185] The electric potential at a distance $r$ from an electric dipole on its axial line varies as:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{1}{r}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{1}{r^3}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$r^2$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{1}{r^2}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, '$V_{\text{axial}} = \frac{1}{4\pi \epsilon_0} \frac{p}{r^2}$.', 'HARD', 'Electrostatics', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000186', 186, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q186] The hybridization and magnetic character of $[\text{Ni}(\text{CN})_4]^{2-}$ complex ion are:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$sp^3$, Paramagnetic"},{"key":"B","text":"$dsp^2$, Paramagnetic"},{"key":"C","text":"$dsp^2$, Diamagnetic"},{"key":"D","text":"$sp^3$, Diamagnetic"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, '$\text{CN}^-$ is a strong field ligand causing pairing of $3d^8$ electrons into square planar $dsp^2$, leaving no unpaired electrons.', 'EASY', 'Coordination Compounds', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000187', 187, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q187] The general solution of the differential equation $\frac{dy}{dx} + y \tan x = \sec x$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$y \\cos x = \\sin x + C$"},{"key":"B","text":"$y \\sec x = \\tan x + C$"},{"key":"C","text":"$y = \\sin x + C \\cos x$"},{"key":"D","text":"$y = \\tan x + C \\sec x$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, '$\text{I.F.} = e^{\int \tan x dx} = \sec x$. Solution is $y \cdot \sec x = \int \sec^2 x dx + C = \tan x + C$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Differential Equations', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000188', 188, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q188] An ideal Carnot heat engine operates between temperatures $500$ K and $300$ K. Its thermal efficiency is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$40\\%$"},{"key":"B","text":"$60\\%$"},{"key":"C","text":"$50\\%$"},{"key":"D","text":"$30\\%$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, '$\eta = 1 - \frac{T_C}{T_H} = 1 - \frac{300}{500} = 0.4 = 40\%$.', 'HARD', 'Thermodynamics', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000189', 189, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q189] For an endothermic reaction to be spontaneous at all temperatures, the change in entropy $\Delta S$ must be:', '[{"key":"A","text":"Negative"},{"key":"B","text":"Zero"},{"key":"C","text":"Always non-spontaneous"},{"key":"D","text":"Positive and $T\\Delta S > \\Delta H$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, '$\Delta G = \Delta H - T\Delta S$. For spontaneity $\Delta G < 0$, requiring $\Delta S > 0$ and $T\Delta S > \Delta H$.', 'EASY', 'Thermodynamics', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000190', 190, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q190] The distance of the point $(1, 2, 3)$ from the plane $2x + y - 2z + 9 = 0$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$2$"},{"key":"B","text":"$7$"},{"key":"C","text":"$3$"},{"key":"D","text":"$1$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, '$d = \frac{|2(1) + 1(2) - 2(3) + 9|}{\sqrt{4+1+4}} = \frac{|2+2-6+9|}{3} = \frac{7}{3}$.', 'MEDIUM', '3D Geometry', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000191', 191, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q191] The escape velocity from the surface of Earth is $11.2$ km/s. If a planet has twice the mass and twice the radius of Earth, its escape velocity is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$22.4$ km/s"},{"key":"B","text":"$11.2$ km/s"},{"key":"C","text":"$5.6$ km/s"},{"key":"D","text":"$15.8$ km/s"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, '$v_e = \sqrt{\frac{2GM}{R}}$. If $M$ and $R$ both double, $M/R$ remains constant, so $v_e$ is unchanged.', 'HARD', 'Gravitation', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000192', 192, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q192] For a first-order reaction $A \to \text{Products}$, the half-life period is $69.3$ minutes. The rate constant $k$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$0.01 \\; \\text{min}^{-1}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$0.1 \\; \\text{min}^{-1}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$0.001 \\; \\text{min}^{-1}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$1.0 \\; \\text{min}^{-1}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, '$k = \frac{0.693}{t_{1/2}} = \frac{0.693}{69.3} = 0.01 \; \text{min}^{-1}$.', 'EASY', 'Chemical Kinetics', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000193', 193, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q193] If $A$ is a $3 \times 3$ non-singular matrix such that $|A| = 4$, then find the value of $|\text{adj}(2A)|$.', '[{"key":"A","text":"1024"},{"key":"B","text":"2048"},{"key":"C","text":"512"},{"key":"D","text":"4096"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, '$|\text{adj}(2A)| = |2A|^{n-1} = (2^3 |A|)^2 = (8 \times 4)^2 = 32^2 = 1024$... check order $n=3$, $(2^3 \cdot 4)^2 = 32^2 = 1024$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Matrices & Determinants', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000194', 194, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q194] A wire of resistance $16 \; \Omega$ is stretched uniformly to twice its original length. The new resistance of the wire will be:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$32 \\; \\Omega$"},{"key":"B","text":"$16 \\; \\Omega$"},{"key":"C","text":"$64 \\; \\Omega$"},{"key":"D","text":"$8 \\; \\Omega$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, '$R \propto l^2$ when volume is conserved. Since length doubles, $R'' = 4 R = 64 \; \Omega$.', 'HARD', 'Current Electricity', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000195', 195, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q195] Which of the following compounds gives a positive Iodoform test upon reaction with $\text{I}_2 / \text{NaOH}$?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Methanol ($\\text{CH}_3\\text{OH}$)"},{"key":"B","text":"Ethanol ($\\text{CH}_3\\text{CH}_2\\text{OH}$)"},{"key":"C","text":"Benzaldehyde"},{"key":"D","text":"Diethyl ether"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'Ethanol has the $\text{CH}_3\text{CH(OH)}-$ unit which oxidizes to acetaldehyde containing $\text{CH}_3\text{C=O}$, giving yellow $\text{CHI}_3$ precipitate.', 'EASY', 'Organic Chemistry (Aldehydes)', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000196', 196, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q196] Two dice are thrown simultaneously. The probability that the sum of the numbers appearing on the dice is a prime number is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{5}{12}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{7}{18}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{1}{3}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{1}{2}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, 'Prime sums: 2 (1), 3 (2), 5 (4), 7 (6), 11 (2) = total 15 outcomes. $P = 15/36 = 5/12$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Probability', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000197', 197, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q197] In Young’s double-slit experiment, if the distance between the slits is halved and the screen distance is doubled, the fringe width becomes:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$2$ times"},{"key":"B","text":"Halved"},{"key":"C","text":"Unchanged"},{"key":"D","text":"$4$ times"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, '$\beta = \frac{\lambda D}{d}$. If $D'' = 2D$ and $d'' = d/2$, $\beta'' = 4 \beta$.', 'HARD', 'Wave Optics', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000198', 198, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q198] The basicity of orthophosphoric acid ($\text{H}_3\text{PO}_4$) is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$2$"},{"key":"B","text":"$1$"},{"key":"C","text":"$3$"},{"key":"D","text":"$4$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, '$\text{H}_3\text{PO}_4$ has three $\text{P-OH}$ ionizable protons, hence basicity is 3.', 'EASY', 'p-Block Elements', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000199', 199, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q199] If $|z - 4/z| = 2$, then the maximum value of $|z|$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\sqrt{5} - 1$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\sqrt{5} + 1$"},{"key":"C","text":"$2\\sqrt{5}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\sqrt{3} + 1$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'By triangle inequality, $|z| - 4/|z| \le |z - 4/z| = 2 \implies |z|^2 - 2|z| - 4 \le 0 \implies |z| \le \sqrt{5}+1$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Complex Numbers', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000200', 200, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q200] A solid sphere and a hollow sphere of equal mass and radius roll down an inclined plane without slipping. The ratio of their accelerations is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{25}{21}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{21}{25}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{15}{14}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{14}{15}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, '$a = \frac{g \sin \theta}{1 + I/(mR^2)}$. For solid: $a_1 = \frac{5}{7}g \sin \theta$. For hollow: $a_2 = \frac{3}{5}g \sin \theta$. Ratio $= \frac{25}{21}$.', 'HARD', 'Rotational Motion', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000201', 201, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q201] Standard electrode potential $E^\circ$ for $\text{Zn}^{2+}/\text{Zn}$ is $-0.76$ V and for $\text{Cu}^{2+}/\text{Cu}$ is $+0.34$ V. The cell EMF $E^\circ_{\text{cell}}$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$-1.10$ V"},{"key":"B","text":"$+0.42$ V"},{"key":"C","text":"$-0.42$ V"},{"key":"D","text":"$+1.10$ V"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, '$E^\circ_{\text{cell}} = E^\circ_{\text{cathode}} - E^\circ_{\text{anode}} = 0.34 - (-0.76) = 1.10$ V.', 'EASY', 'Electrochemistry', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000202', 202, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q202] Let $\vec{a} = 2\hat{i} + \hat{j} - 2\hat{k}$ and $\vec{b} = \hat{i} + \hat{j}$. The projection of $\vec{a}$ along $\vec{b}$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{3}{2}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\sqrt{2}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$3\\sqrt{2}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, '$\text{proj}_{\vec{b}} \vec{a} = \frac{\vec{a} \cdot \vec{b}}{|\vec{b}|} = \frac{2(1) + 1(1) + 0}{\sqrt{1^2+1^2}} = \frac{3}{\sqrt{2}}$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Vector Algebra', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000203', 203, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q203] The magnetic flux linked with a coil varies with time as $\Phi = 4t^3 - 2t + 5$ Wb. The magnitude of induced EMF at $t = 2$ s is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$48$ V"},{"key":"B","text":"$46$ V"},{"key":"C","text":"$50$ V"},{"key":"D","text":"$44$ V"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, '$e = |-\frac{d\Phi}{dt}| = |12t^2 - 2|$. At $t=2$, $e = 12(4) - 2 = 46$ V.', 'HARD', 'Electromagnetic Induction', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000204', 204, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q204] The van ''t Hoff factor $i$ for a dilute aqueous solution of barium chloride $\text{BaCl}_2$ assuming complete dissociation is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$3$"},{"key":"B","text":"$2$"},{"key":"C","text":"$1$"},{"key":"D","text":"$4$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, '$\text{BaCl}_2 \to \text{Ba}^{2+} + 2\text{Cl}^-$, producing 3 ions per formula unit.', 'EASY', 'Solutions', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000205', 205, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q205] Evaluate: $\lim_{x \to 0} \frac{e^{\sin x} - 1 - \sin x}{x^2}$.', '[{"key":"A","text":"$1$"},{"key":"B","text":"$0$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{1}{4}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{1}{2}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, 'Using series expansion $e^t = 1 + t + \frac{t^2}{2!} + \dots$, $\frac{t^2/2}{x^2} \to 1/2$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Limits & Continuity', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000206', 206, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q206] The de Broglie wavelength of an electron accelerated through a potential difference of $100$ V is approximately:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$1.23$ nm"},{"key":"B","text":"$0.012$ nm"},{"key":"C","text":"$0.123$ nm"},{"key":"D","text":"$12.3$ nm"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, '$\lambda = \frac{1.227}{\sqrt{V}}$ nm $= \frac{1.227}{10} = 0.123$ nm.', 'HARD', 'Modern Physics', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000207', 207, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q207] Which of the following nitrogenous bases is found in RNA but not in DNA?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Thymine"},{"key":"B","text":"Uracil"},{"key":"C","text":"Guanine"},{"key":"D","text":"Cytosine"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'RNA contains Uracil instead of Thymine.', 'EASY', 'Biomolecules', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000208', 208, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q208] Evaluate the definite integral: $I = \int_{0}^{\pi/2} \frac{\sin^3 x}{\sin^3 x + \cos^3 x} dx$', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\pi$"},{"key":"D","text":"$0$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, 'By applying property $\int_a^b f(x)dx = \int_a^b f(a+b-x)dx$, $2I = \int_0^{\pi/2} 1 dx = \frac{\pi}{2} \implies I = \frac{\pi}{4}$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Definite Integrals', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000209', 209, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q209] The electric potential at a distance $r$ from an electric dipole on its axial line varies as:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{1}{r}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{1}{r^3}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$r^2$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{1}{r^2}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, '$V_{\text{axial}} = \frac{1}{4\pi \epsilon_0} \frac{p}{r^2}$.', 'HARD', 'Electrostatics', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000210', 210, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q210] The hybridization and magnetic character of $[\text{Ni}(\text{CN})_4]^{2-}$ complex ion are:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$sp^3$, Paramagnetic"},{"key":"B","text":"$dsp^2$, Paramagnetic"},{"key":"C","text":"$dsp^2$, Diamagnetic"},{"key":"D","text":"$sp^3$, Diamagnetic"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, '$\text{CN}^-$ is a strong field ligand causing pairing of $3d^8$ electrons into square planar $dsp^2$, leaving no unpaired electrons.', 'EASY', 'Coordination Compounds', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000211', 211, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q211] The general solution of the differential equation $\frac{dy}{dx} + y \tan x = \sec x$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$y \\cos x = \\sin x + C$"},{"key":"B","text":"$y \\sec x = \\tan x + C$"},{"key":"C","text":"$y = \\sin x + C \\cos x$"},{"key":"D","text":"$y = \\tan x + C \\sec x$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, '$\text{I.F.} = e^{\int \tan x dx} = \sec x$. Solution is $y \cdot \sec x = \int \sec^2 x dx + C = \tan x + C$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Differential Equations', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000212', 212, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q212] An ideal Carnot heat engine operates between temperatures $500$ K and $300$ K. Its thermal efficiency is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$40\\%$"},{"key":"B","text":"$60\\%$"},{"key":"C","text":"$50\\%$"},{"key":"D","text":"$30\\%$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, '$\eta = 1 - \frac{T_C}{T_H} = 1 - \frac{300}{500} = 0.4 = 40\%$.', 'HARD', 'Thermodynamics', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000213', 213, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q213] For an endothermic reaction to be spontaneous at all temperatures, the change in entropy $\Delta S$ must be:', '[{"key":"A","text":"Negative"},{"key":"B","text":"Zero"},{"key":"C","text":"Always non-spontaneous"},{"key":"D","text":"Positive and $T\\Delta S > \\Delta H$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, '$\Delta G = \Delta H - T\Delta S$. For spontaneity $\Delta G < 0$, requiring $\Delta S > 0$ and $T\Delta S > \Delta H$.', 'EASY', 'Thermodynamics', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000214', 214, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q214] The distance of the point $(1, 2, 3)$ from the plane $2x + y - 2z + 9 = 0$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$2$"},{"key":"B","text":"$7$"},{"key":"C","text":"$3$"},{"key":"D","text":"$1$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, '$d = \frac{|2(1) + 1(2) - 2(3) + 9|}{\sqrt{4+1+4}} = \frac{|2+2-6+9|}{3} = \frac{7}{3}$.', 'MEDIUM', '3D Geometry', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000215', 215, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q215] The escape velocity from the surface of Earth is $11.2$ km/s. If a planet has twice the mass and twice the radius of Earth, its escape velocity is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$22.4$ km/s"},{"key":"B","text":"$11.2$ km/s"},{"key":"C","text":"$5.6$ km/s"},{"key":"D","text":"$15.8$ km/s"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, '$v_e = \sqrt{\frac{2GM}{R}}$. If $M$ and $R$ both double, $M/R$ remains constant, so $v_e$ is unchanged.', 'HARD', 'Gravitation', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000216', 216, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q216] For a first-order reaction $A \to \text{Products}$, the half-life period is $69.3$ minutes. The rate constant $k$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$0.01 \\; \\text{min}^{-1}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$0.1 \\; \\text{min}^{-1}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$0.001 \\; \\text{min}^{-1}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$1.0 \\; \\text{min}^{-1}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, '$k = \frac{0.693}{t_{1/2}} = \frac{0.693}{69.3} = 0.01 \; \text{min}^{-1}$.', 'EASY', 'Chemical Kinetics', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000217', 217, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q217] If $A$ is a $3 \times 3$ non-singular matrix such that $|A| = 4$, then find the value of $|\text{adj}(2A)|$.', '[{"key":"A","text":"1024"},{"key":"B","text":"2048"},{"key":"C","text":"512"},{"key":"D","text":"4096"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, '$|\text{adj}(2A)| = |2A|^{n-1} = (2^3 |A|)^2 = (8 \times 4)^2 = 32^2 = 1024$... check order $n=3$, $(2^3 \cdot 4)^2 = 32^2 = 1024$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Matrices & Determinants', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000218', 218, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q218] A wire of resistance $16 \; \Omega$ is stretched uniformly to twice its original length. The new resistance of the wire will be:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$32 \\; \\Omega$"},{"key":"B","text":"$16 \\; \\Omega$"},{"key":"C","text":"$64 \\; \\Omega$"},{"key":"D","text":"$8 \\; \\Omega$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, '$R \propto l^2$ when volume is conserved. Since length doubles, $R'' = 4 R = 64 \; \Omega$.', 'HARD', 'Current Electricity', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000219', 219, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q219] Which of the following compounds gives a positive Iodoform test upon reaction with $\text{I}_2 / \text{NaOH}$?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Methanol ($\\text{CH}_3\\text{OH}$)"},{"key":"B","text":"Ethanol ($\\text{CH}_3\\text{CH}_2\\text{OH}$)"},{"key":"C","text":"Benzaldehyde"},{"key":"D","text":"Diethyl ether"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'Ethanol has the $\text{CH}_3\text{CH(OH)}-$ unit which oxidizes to acetaldehyde containing $\text{CH}_3\text{C=O}$, giving yellow $\text{CHI}_3$ precipitate.', 'EASY', 'Organic Chemistry (Aldehydes)', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000220', 220, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q220] Two dice are thrown simultaneously. The probability that the sum of the numbers appearing on the dice is a prime number is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{5}{12}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{7}{18}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{1}{3}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{1}{2}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, 'Prime sums: 2 (1), 3 (2), 5 (4), 7 (6), 11 (2) = total 15 outcomes. $P = 15/36 = 5/12$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Probability', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000221', 221, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q221] In Young’s double-slit experiment, if the distance between the slits is halved and the screen distance is doubled, the fringe width becomes:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$2$ times"},{"key":"B","text":"Halved"},{"key":"C","text":"Unchanged"},{"key":"D","text":"$4$ times"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, '$\beta = \frac{\lambda D}{d}$. If $D'' = 2D$ and $d'' = d/2$, $\beta'' = 4 \beta$.', 'HARD', 'Wave Optics', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000222', 222, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q222] The basicity of orthophosphoric acid ($\text{H}_3\text{PO}_4$) is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$2$"},{"key":"B","text":"$1$"},{"key":"C","text":"$3$"},{"key":"D","text":"$4$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, '$\text{H}_3\text{PO}_4$ has three $\text{P-OH}$ ionizable protons, hence basicity is 3.', 'EASY', 'p-Block Elements', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000223', 223, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q223] If $|z - 4/z| = 2$, then the maximum value of $|z|$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\sqrt{5} - 1$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\sqrt{5} + 1$"},{"key":"C","text":"$2\\sqrt{5}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\sqrt{3} + 1$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, 'By triangle inequality, $|z| - 4/|z| \le |z - 4/z| = 2 \implies |z|^2 - 2|z| - 4 \le 0 \implies |z| \le \sqrt{5}+1$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Complex Numbers', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000224', 224, '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'Physics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q224] A solid sphere and a hollow sphere of equal mass and radius roll down an inclined plane without slipping. The ratio of their accelerations is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{25}{21}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{21}{25}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{15}{14}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{14}{15}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"A","key":"A"}'::jsonb, '$a = \frac{g \sin \theta}{1 + I/(mR^2)}$. For solid: $a_1 = \frac{5}{7}g \sin \theta$. For hollow: $a_2 = \frac{3}{5}g \sin \theta$. Ratio $= \frac{25}{21}$.', 'HARD', 'Rotational Motion', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000225', 225, 'd7e1c77a-3837-4f8a-a673-5c852bd356ab', 'Chemistry', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q225] Standard electrode potential $E^\circ$ for $\text{Zn}^{2+}/\text{Zn}$ is $-0.76$ V and for $\text{Cu}^{2+}/\text{Cu}$ is $+0.34$ V. The cell EMF $E^\circ_{\text{cell}}$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$-1.10$ V"},{"key":"B","text":"$+0.42$ V"},{"key":"C","text":"$-0.42$ V"},{"key":"D","text":"$+1.10$ V"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, '$E^\circ_{\text{cell}} = E^\circ_{\text{cathode}} - E^\circ_{\text{anode}} = 0.34 - (-0.76) = 1.10$ V.', 'EASY', 'Electrochemistry', NULL),
  ('e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000226', 226, '50a02b50-667d-4beb-add5-a05a11204e9a', 'Mathematics', 'MCQ', 4, 1, '[Q226] Let $\vec{a} = 2\hat{i} + \hat{j} - 2\hat{k}$ and $\vec{b} = \hat{i} + \hat{j}$. The projection of $\vec{a}$ along $\vec{b}$ is:', '[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{3}{2}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\sqrt{2}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$3\\sqrt{2}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, '$\text{proj}_{\vec{b}} \vec{a} = \frac{\vec{a} \cdot \vec{b}}{|\vec{b}|} = \frac{2(1) + 1(1) + 0}{\sqrt{1^2+1^2}} = \frac{3}{\sqrt{2}}$.', 'MEDIUM', 'Vector Algebra', NULL),
